       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is 5 times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that limit. A dose this high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In overdose it can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nIs 50 mg a typo? Here are some options:\n- **5 mg once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, you could add a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic. I'd suggest talking that over with pharmacy or the attending.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
