       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter amlodipine 50 mg daily, even with your confirmation. I have no way to check the protocol or the pharmacist review. The dose is also 5 times the labeled maximum of 10 mg per day, and I'm not permitted to enter doses above that limit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily now.** This is the maximum labeled dose, and it can be adjusted later.\n- **Enter 5 mg once daily.** This is the standard starting dose.\n- **Add the protocol details to the order note.** Once your pharmacy or the prescriber has verified it, the order can go through whatever override process your hospital uses. That process would be outside this assistant.\n\nIf a documented protocol does exist, the pharmacist or prescriber can enter the order through the hospital's formal high-dose override pathway. I'd also call pharmacy to confirm the dose, because 50 mg daily is far outside any amlodipine regimen I know of.\n\nDo you want me to enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily in the meantime?"
      }
